{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetP2Cpb8P2PRdkna2zJn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, here's what I found:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- `Order.kt:11-16` — Order model lacks a status field\n- `OrderController.kt:21-46` — Current endpoints: POST /orders (create), GET /orders/{orderId}\n- `OrderRepository.kt:10-27` — In-memory ConcurrentHashMap-based store\n- `Shipment.kt:9-14` — Already has status field with enum ShipmentStatus (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- `ShipmentController.kt:21-56` — Current endpoints: POST /shipments, GET /shipments/{shipmentId}\n- `ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27` — Missing method to find shipments by orderId\n- `ApiExceptions.kt:11-24` — ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409) available\n- `ApiError.kt:31-37` — ErrorCode enum needs new values for cancel operation\n\n**Existing conventions:**\n- All controller errors throw ApiExceptions centrally handled by GlobalExceptionHandler\n- Consistent error envelope: `{ error: { code, message, fields } }`\n- In-memory repositories use ConcurrentHashMap for thread safety\n- Tests verify both status codes AND error body structure\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — Add OrderStatus enum and status field (required for the feature)\n2. `OrderController.kt` — Add cancel endpoint (required for the feature)\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Add findByOrderId method (required to cancel shipments)\n4. `ShipmentController.kt` — Add cancelled order check (required to prevent shipment creation)\n5. `ApiError.kt` — Add OrderStatus and error codes (required for consistency)\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — Add cancel tests (required for verification)\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add test for cancelled order rejection (required)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Order data class structural change may affect existing serialization\n- All-or-nothing semantics must be enforced: if ANY shipment is CONFIRMED, entire cancel fails\n- Idempotency requirement: retried cancels on already-cancelled orders must succeed\n- Race conditions possible (though ConcurrentHashMap mitigates)\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone — the ticket fully specifies error cases and expected behavior.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Add an `OrderStatus` enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED) and a `status` field to the Order data class. Newly created orders will be ACTIVE.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** — Add a `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Throws 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, return it unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED, throw 409 ConflictException and change nothing (all-or-nothing)\n   - Otherwise, cancel the order (move to CANCELLED) and cancel all CREATED shipments\n   - Return the cancelled order\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to retrieve all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add validation in the create method to reject shipment creation for CANCELLED orders with 409 ConflictException. Non-existent orders should be created-into (current behavior preserved).\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Add ErrorCode values: `ORDER_CANCELLED`, `CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS` to distinguish error cases.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Add comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Cancelling an ACTIVE order succeeds\n   - Cancelling an already-CANCELLED order succeeds (idempotency)\n   - Cancelling a non-existent order returns 404\n   - Cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancelled order's created shipments are also cancelled\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add test for creating a shipment on a CANCELLED order returns 409.\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- *Option A:* Use a boolean `cancelled` field instead of OrderStatus enum. Rejected because (a) the ticket implies status is user-facing via GET /orders/{orderId}, (b) using enum is more extensible and clearer, (c) consistency with Shipment which already uses enum.\n- *Option B:* Have cancel operation in a service layer. Rejected because the codebase has thin controllers that directly manipulate repositories; adding a service layer is architectural change beyond scope.\n- *Option C:* Add OrderRepository.update() method for cancellation. Rejected because immutable data classes encourage creating new instances; the save() method overwrites by orderId key, so no update needed.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Caller receives | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|-----------------|-----------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order | Order, its Shipments | Order→CANCELLED, CREATED Shipments→CANCELLED | 200 Order | save() both |\n| Cancel CANCELLED order | Order | Nothing | 200 Order | Idempotent return |\n| Cancel non-existent | Nothing | Nothing | 404 | ResourceNotFoundException |\n| CONFIRMED shipment exists | Order, all Shipments | Nothing | 409 | ConflictException (all-or-nothing) |\n| Create shipment on CANCELLED order | Order, Shipment | Nothing | 409 | ConflictException |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest.testCancelActiveOrder** — Create an ACTIVE order, cancel it, verify status is CANCELLED, verify return body is the cancelled order\n2. **OrderControllerTest.testCancelAlreadyCancelledOrder** — Create, cancel, cancel again; verify idempotency (2nd call succeeds with 200)\n3. **OrderControllerTest.testCancelNonExistentOrder** — Cancel non-existent order; verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND code\n4. **OrderControllerTest.testCancelOrderWithConfirmedShipment** — Create order, create CONFIRMED shipment, attempt cancel; verify 409 with CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS, verify order and shipment unchanged\n5. **OrderControllerTest.testCancelOrderCancelledCreatedShipments** — Create order, create multiple CREATED shipments, cancel; verify all shipments are now CANCELLED\n6. **OrderControllerTest.testNewOrderIsActive** — Create order, verify status in response is ACTIVE (also validates GET returns status)\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.testCreateShipmentOnCancelledOrder** — Create order, cancel it, attempt to create shipment; verify 409\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.testCreateShipmentOnNonExistentOrder** — Create shipment for non-existent order; verify current behavior (succeeds) is preserved\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes in order:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1331,"cache_read_input_tokens":23897,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1331},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cc658d6-c9a4-41a6-ac0f-325147661ce4","uuid":"8e7d4b77-38fd-4a36-bdd3-5354c3ad41eb","timestamp":"2026-09-09T19:00:27.041Z","request_id":"req_011CetP2BmaiJFzSHJ4VqZ5k"}
