: yes, core feature.\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added findByOrderId method. Required: yes, needed to query shipments by order during cancel.\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders. Required: yes, enforces constraint.\n5. **ApiError.kt** — Added ORDER_CANCELLED and CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS error codes. Required: yes, for error differentiation.\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 8 comprehensive tests. Required: yes, for verification.\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 2 tests for cancelled order rejection. Required: yes, for verification.\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All ticket requirements are implemented and tested.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint to cancel active orders, cancel their CREATED shipments, with idempotent behavior for already-cancelled orders and all-or-nothing semantics for CONFIRMED shipments.\n\nChanged       Order.kt (added OrderStatus enum and status field)\n              OrderController.kt (added cancel endpoint with conflict checks and shipment cancellation)\n              ShipmentRepository.kt (added findByOrderId method)\n              ShipmentController.kt (added cancelled order validation)\n              ApiError.kt (added ORDER_CANCELLED and CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS error codes)\n              OrderControllerTest.kt (added 8 tests for cancel scenarios)\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt (added 2 tests for cancelled order rejection)\n\nTests         testNewOrderIsActive — verifies new orders have ACTIVE status\n              testCancelActiveOrder — cancels ACTIVE order, returns CANCELLED order with 200\n              testReadingCancelledOrder — GET returns CANCELLED status after cancel\n              testCancelAlreadyCancelledOrder — idempotency: second cancel succeeds with 200\n              testCancelNonExistentOrder — missing order returns 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n              testCancelOrderWithConfirmedShipment — CONFIRMED shipment blocks cancel with 409, changes nothing\n              testCancelOrderCancelledCreatedShipments — CREATED shipments moved to CANCELLED\n              testCancelOrderLeavesOtherShipmentsUnchanged — only cancelled order's shipments affected\n              testCreateShipmentForNonExistentOrder — preserves current behavior (succeeds)\n              testRejectCreateShipmentForCancelledOrder — 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED when order is CANCELLED\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test\n              Result: 23 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors (13 existing + 10 new)\n              Build: SUCCESS\n\nNot done      Nothing — all acceptance criteria satisfied, all tests passing, no unrelated changes made.\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2917,"cache_read_input_tokens":39082,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2917},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cc658d6-c9a4-41a6-ac0f-325147661ce4","uuid":"fb027876-5f1c-4f1c-a755-657b2e79d6be","timestamp":"2026-09-09T19:02:16.066Z","request_id":"req_011CetPAszFnxqddBE1wDg5S"}
